Done. All gates pass on the shipped file, and the layer + record are in place.

**One-line report:** Technique: adoptable layout library (`#define GEN_LAYOUT_LIB_ONLY` + `#include "gen_layout.c"` — THP arenas, 4672B-stagger takes, mod-4096 collision model generalized from L17's astab, far-phase dynamic placement, AVX-512 pencil/lane-SoA pack) plus an any-L (2–128) dense matrixsimd demo entry exercising it; best node timings per transform: L=12 15.71 µs at B=1 / 16.05 µs at B=64 (L=32: 478.5 µs B=1 / 500.0 µs B=8; 7–11.5× the scalar floor), rel L2 = 3.1e-16 at L=12 (worst 6.5e-16 at L=100, map-chain m=600 5.1e-14 vs 1e-10 tol).

Details for the record:

- **Library**: `gl_map_huge`/`gl_arena_*` (prefaulted 2MiB THP, per-take phase rotation), `gl_phase4k`/`gl_far_phase4k`/`gl_arena_take_phase` (deterministic placement), `gl_alias_pairs4k`/`gl_best_lineshift4k`/`gl_walk_min_gap4k` (the collision model — verified it reproduces L17's result: shift 5 takes the 5120-vs-4624-stride geometry from 9 alias pairs to 0), `gl_pack8`/`gl_unpack8`/`gl_tr8x8`/`gl_deint8`/`gl_int8` (SoA converters with `gl_selftest`), scalar fallbacks so adopters build on any host. Adopter-style include-test compiles `-Wall -Wextra` clean on both wallaby (AVX2) and a80n0 (AVX-512).
- **Honest null result, recorded prominently**: on the compute-bound demo, every layout knob — THP vs plain, placement off, even adversarial same-phase collision — is within noise (≤0.8%). The record explains why (pencil-block staging decouples the aliasing streams) and cites the ice cases where placement was worth double digits, so class owners treat the tools as free insurance verified by the model, not superstition.
- **Harness bugs found and documented for the panel**: `tryout.sh` uses `$W` before defining it (kills every m>1 case under `set -u`; workaround: pre-export `W`), the same hole silently skips the remote map-check and MKL reference, and `reserve.sh --status` needs `/opt/software/slurm-19.05.8.1/bin` on PATH on wallaby (the reservation was alive all along; I re-verified via heartbeat and squeue).
